# Keep the Docker build context small.
#
# The dev gateway builds with the repo root as its context (it needs the
# backend source trees), and the repo also holds the raw datasets: WLASL alone
# is a 1.2 GB archive plus 8,810 keypoint folders, and dictionary/ is another
# 276 MB. Docker uploads the entire context to the daemon before running the
# first instruction, so without this file a one-minute build spends many
# minutes transferring data that no image ever uses.
#
# Anything the containers actually need at runtime is bind-mounted by
# dev/docker-compose.yml, not copied in.

# ── Raw datasets and derived clips (bind-mounted, never COPYed) ──────────────
WLASL/
datasets/
data/
dictionary/

# ── Build outputs and dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
extension/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# ── Local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.env.local
**/*.log
